WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
Though we cannot have
actual real audiences

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.343
because of course the COVID epidemic,

00:00:09.198 --> 00:00:10.810
we do have cutouts.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.050
I mentioned this earlier in the week.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.110
Random cutouts that we found

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.770
in a storage room on the
Warner Brother's lot.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.120
Here they are joining us,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.560
a cutout of Ruth Bader Ginsburg,

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.400
the Supreme Court Justice,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.220
Conrad Bain, the father
on Different Strokes.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.480
We have a life-sized, six-foot-six

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.150
cutout of former FBI director James Comey.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.910
And four, count them four Kevin Harts.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.610
So we got that.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.720
All right, we are not alone.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.040
Also I should point out,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.140
she's either a cutout or a real person,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.290
my assistant Sona Movsesian.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.440
Sona!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.920
Oh yeah, I saw your head move,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.540
you are the real Sona.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.496
Yeah I'm real.

00:00:54.496 --> 00:00:55.647
[Conan] Okay, how are you?

00:00:55.647 --> 00:00:57.180
I'm all right, how are you?

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.500
[Conan] You enjoy being in a crowd?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.190
Is there a feeling of
electricity in that crowd?

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.656
No it's kinda sad and lonely actually.

00:01:03.656 --> 00:01:06.730
It's a little depressing out here.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.890
Thank you!

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.720
Thank you for pumping up the show, Sona.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.420
Great job. Lonely and depressing.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.870
Everything I just did to create a sense

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:21.890
of visceral excitement
now deflated, right Sona?

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.791
Yeah, its really just, there's nothing-

00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:27.300
Got it!

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.380
Thank you, thank you.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.464
Good to have you here, as always.

00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:34.297
There's no one else here.

00:01:34.297 --> 00:01:35.611
We're good!

00:01:35.611 --> 00:01:37.510
I'm just by myself.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.880
Okay! We got it, all by
yourself and depressed.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.010
Hey! Guess what?

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.571
I think we're all feeling that
way, don't you think Sona?

00:01:46.571 --> 00:01:47.920
Don't you think a lot of people

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.200
are feeling a little down these days?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.323
Yeah, I think there's a lot of depression.

00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:54.822
Yeah, I can't hear you, its the mask.

00:01:54.822 --> 00:01:57.104
You sound like one of the parents

00:01:57.104 --> 00:01:59.317
on a Charlie Brown cartoon.

00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:00.777
(Sona laughing)

00:02:00.777 --> 00:02:01.610
But anyway

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.960
(cartoon mumbling)

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.370
You know, we are in the middle

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.410
of a global pandemic,
no getting around that.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.730
And you may have seen

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:09.950
a lot of the critical data

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.990
that's been charted
and graphed by the CDC.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.840
Okay, and that's fine, that's good.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.120
We need science, we need information.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.370
But as I've mentioned,

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.720
some of the graphs that they're releasing

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.699
seem a little unnecessary,

00:02:22.699 --> 00:02:25.100
as far a I'm concerned.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.210
For example, I don't know

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.340
if you've seen this one,

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:30.611
since March, there's been a 98% increase

00:02:30.611 --> 00:02:32.650
in Americans walking
into their living rooms,

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.507
stopping and saying,
"why did I come in here?"

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.270
Yeah, there's been a 68% increase

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.810
in deciding not to learn

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:43.500
another language after all.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.080
There's been a 60% increase

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.480
in horny guys bragging

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.347
that their oxygen sat rates are

00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:50.517
"...through the roof, bro!"

00:02:51.731 --> 00:02:53.507
How are these so far, Sona?

00:02:53.507 --> 00:02:57.913
They're good. They're
really funny, nice job.

00:02:59.256 --> 00:03:01.020
Jesus Christ.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.610
Hey, there's been a 438% decrease

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.213
in your dog's interest in you.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.570
There's been a 70% increase

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.750
in asking the Postmates
person to hold you gently.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.740
There's been a non-stop increase

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.683
in aimless walks taken.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.977
There's been a significant
increase in Americans saying,

00:03:18.977 --> 00:03:23.150
"Might as well try that
Elon Musk brain chip."

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:26.430
And finally, a chart depicting my binges:

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.790
food, Netflix,

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.863
and sex.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:32.693
See how that last one,

00:03:32.693 --> 00:03:34.035
kind of the joke was on me?

00:03:34.035 --> 00:03:38.720
Yeah. Yeah that was good.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.223
That was funny.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.835
My own fault for asking Sona's opinion.

00:03:43.835 --> 00:03:44.955
No one needs to know.

00:03:44.955 --> 00:03:46.987
No one needs to know that, and by the way

00:03:46.987 --> 00:03:48.107
(laughs)

00:03:48.107 --> 00:03:51.400
okay? Lets just say this guy...

00:03:52.384 --> 00:03:53.383
[Sona] What?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.133
Anyway!

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.676
(Sona laughing)

